       "text": "I didn't enter this order. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is far above the labeled maximum of 200 mg per day, which is five times the limit. A dose that high risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity.\n\nWas 1000 mg a typo? Here are some options:\n- **100 mg once daily.** This is a common maintenance dose.\n- **50 mg once daily.** This is the usual starting dose for depression.\n- **200 mg once daily.** This is the maximum labeled dose, and it's usually reached by titrating up.\n\nTell me the dose and indication you want, and I'll enter the order. If you really do intend a dose above the labeled maximum, it will need to go through pharmacy and prescriber review outside this system. I can't enter it on my own."
      }
