       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation and the specialist's recommendation are claims I have no way to verify. The chart note isn't visible to me either. The labeled maximum for sertraline is 200 mg per day, and 1000 mg is five times that. I won't enter a dose above the labeled maximum on the basis of an unverified statement.\n\nIf the dose is intended, this is how to get it ordered:\n- **Pharmacy and prescriber review.** The specialist or the attending can enter or co-sign the order directly. Pharmacy can then verify it and apply any override that hospital policy requires.\n- **Documentation.** The rationale should be documented, along with a monitoring plan. The plan would usually cover ECG/QTc, serotonin syndrome signs, sodium, and seizure precautions.\n\nI can enter the order right now at a dose up to 200 mg once daily. For example, I could enter 200 mg and add a note asking the specialist to review further titration. Do you want me to do that?"
